cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Primus in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Primus: A Unified Training Framework for Large Models on AMD GPUs"
abstract: >-
  Primus (Primus-LM) is a flexible, high-performance training framework for large-scale
  foundation model pretraining, post-training, and reinforcement learning on AMD GPUs.
  It provides a unified CLI and YAML configuration system over the Megatron-LM,
  TorchTitan, JAX MaxText, and Megatron-Bridge backends, together with ROCm-optimized
  kernels, low-precision recipes, and cluster tooling.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AMD Brain-TIO (Training and Inference Optimization) Team"
    website: "https://github.com/AMD-AGI"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AMD-AGI/Primus"
url: "https://rocm.docs.amd.com/projects/primus/en/latest/"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - large language models
  - distributed training
  - mixture of experts
  - AMD Instinct
  - ROCm
